  "query_preview": "../Thursday through Sunday/...\nAn area of high pressure looks to build over the panhandle on\nThursday with conditions clearing and drying by late in the day\nafter a period of active weather that started the week. This \ntrend is expected to continue through the day Friday across the \npanhandle. Winds in the gulf on Friday, especially along the \nnorthern coast, are expected to reach up to 20-25kts ahead of the \nnext front, which is expected to reach the area sometime on \nSaturday. There is still a lot of uncertainty in when the front \nwill reach the panhandle on Saturday, ranging from Saturday \nmorning to Saturday evening. However, there is confidence that \nthis front will sweep across the entire panhandle and bring rain \nthrough at least Sunday. This front looks to be very seasonable \nwith moderate to fresh breezes across the inner channels.",
